BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Detail: The webhook passes the inbound call UUID, the E.164 phone number, the campaign tag, and the state. Every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (dial should record the entire call for later reference [Carlos Corona - tf4AieS7Mhc @ 00:08:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (Carlos Corona's ACA flow is the most complete pay-per-call build in this chapter, and it runs on two keypad prompts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (The opening message reads: We are one step closer to getting you approved for help with gas, groceries, and rent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (Please press two if you do not have Medicare, Medicaid, or employer coverage. Please press one if you do have it. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (press of two qualifies the caller and kicks off the RTB process to the buyers on the routing plan [tf4AieS7Mhc @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (00:01:22]. A press of one does not end the call. Corona replays a longer version that opens with: please listen carefully) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (as our menu has changed. The replay splits into one for Medicaid, two for Medicare, and three for no government) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (health benefits, and a press of three routes back to the buyers [tf4AieS7Mhc @ 00:01:55]. His reason comes straight) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (from live traffic. A lot of people press something that was not the correct answer, and the second pass gives them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (another chance to make the right choice [tf4AieS7Mhc @ 00:02:30]. SignalWire's Nicholas builds the same safety net) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (generically. An attempt variable increments each time the gather times out or receives unknown input. A short audio) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (cue plays before the caller loops back to the prompt. After two failed attempts, the flow disconnects the call) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm ([VByuomL6T0s @ 00:05:14].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (Corona treats callers who confirm Medicaid or Medicare as no-value calls. Instead of hanging up on them, he converts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (them into an SMS opt-in. He builds a gather that accepts only a press of one. He lists the elements an IVR consent has) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (to carry: the brand name, how to opt out, where to see the terms, and that message rates apply [tf4AieS7Mhc @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (00:05:10]. His live script reads: Thank you for calling Medicare benefits. All agents are busy. Press one to complete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (your request via text. By pressing one, you agree to automated texts. To opt out, reply stop. Message rates apply. For) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (terms, visit medicarebenefits.net/terms [tf4AieS7Mhc @ 00:06:06]. A press of one fires a webhook with four fields: the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (inbound call UUID for reference if issues come up, the phone number in E.164 format for later texting, a campaign tag,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (and the state for time zones. The flow then dials a confirmation routing plan whose target only plays a message-sent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (prompt, and every dial records the entire call [tf4AieS7Mhc @ 00:08:44]. Henryk Brzozowski's Retell AI setup shows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (the webhook limits operators must design around. The timeout is 10 seconds, with up to three retries before a silent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (fallback to the default agent. He also whitelists IPs so only Retell can reach his make.com endpoint [p7WavoW_6to @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (00:04:24].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (Ringba's node set is the toolkit most of these pay-per-call builds run on. The dial node routes to a target, and the menu) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (node decides on the key pressed. The router node decides on filters, and the gather node collects numerical input. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (hours node routes on hours of operation, and the pixel node fires pixels from inside the call flow. The JS node runs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (custom JavaScript once the team activates it, and the profile node pulls enriched caller data [Ua5XxaPrhRs @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (00:03:42]. The robocall verification template asks every caller to press one to continue and automatically terminates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (anything that cannot, so spam robocallers never reach targets [Ua5XxaPrhRs @ 00:04:54]. On the buyer side, Shane) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (Hitchcock explains Dial IVR. The operator times how long a buyer's own IVR takes to ask for a keypress and enters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (that timing. Ringba then sends the DTMF digit, or a dynamic tag such as a zip code, without the caller hearing it) Tj ET
