BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 445.77 Tm (The Integrity Connect inbound program punishes picky agents by the numbers. Trey and Shanti Berlin of Ringba) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 430.55 Tm (explain that a $5 revenue per call forces publishers to produce calls for about $4, while a $20 RPC lets them spend) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 415.32 Tm (about $17 per call, so cherry-picking directly degrades traffic [N3imbfBa8rI @ 00:14:24]. Rejecting good prospects) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 400.10 Tm (trains the algorithm toward worse calls, and the AI flags a buyer after roughly 30 calls with no conversion. Over a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 384.87 Tm (50-call running total, an RPC under $5, possibly raised to $8, gets the agent turned off, and penalties escalate from a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 369.65 Tm (temporary pause to a one-week pause to removal [N3imbfBa8rI @ 00:26:18]. Adeline puts the floor near $9 and runs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 354.42 Tm (about $18 RPC by taking roughly 40 percent of calls [-YRrdoKG1xs @ 00:07:47]. The math is explicit: at a $50) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 339.20 Tm (billable call with one in five taken, the publisher earns $10 per call and must generate calls for $6 to $8, while taking) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 323.97 Tm (half unlocks the $15 to $20 calls [-YRrdoKG1xs @ 00:12:11]. Adeline's first week still produced 20-plus billable calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 308.75 Tm (and only one sale before Adeline went back to Go Leads. The same training flags rudeness, profanity, pushing 'this isn't) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 293.52 Tm (free,' and impersonating the Department of Insurance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 278.30 Tm (Lead and transfer quality fails in predictable ways. Willie Goldberg's two-week test of 49 transfers at $25 each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 263.07 Tm (produced 5 sales, roughly one in ten, putting cost per sale near $250 to $300, and the ACA pool was cut after a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.85 Tm (term sale [A4zDgHX2VWI @ 00:01:15]. Goldberg's bigger warning is vendors reselling sold leads and recycling them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 232.62 Tm (within 30, 60, or 90 days, which means lower persistency and more replacement, plus ads that mislead with free, Social) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 217.40 Tm (Security, or VA claims, which Goldberg calls a very shady practice [A4zDgHX2VWI @ 00:09:22]. Tyler Glennon hits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 202.17 Tm (the same mismatch from the agent chair: some ads promise accidental coverage at $500,000 for about $25 a month, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 186.95 Tm (the agent must redirect to real coverage or sell accidental as a fallback because the lead is already paid for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 171.72 Tm ([LvZ0uD7-Xvs @ 00:05:08]. Carlos Corona's own scars are operational: a flights campaign built on Google showed) Tj ET
